# Neon Pairs

A silent, offline memory game built from the [version 2.2 specification](docs/README.md).

Use Node.js 24.19 or later and npm. The named compatibility combination is Node
26.12.1, npm 11.20.0, Playwright 1.64.1 and Chromium 156.0.8078.4. Dependencies are
exactly pinned in `package.json` and `package-lock.json`.

```sh
npm ci
npm run dev
npm run typecheck
npm test
npx playwright install chromium
npm run test:e2e
npm run build
```

`npm run test:e2e` first type checks and builds the current source, and stops if
that build fails. Playwright starts a local server for that build and uses fresh
browser contexts. `npm run build` produces `dist/index.html`, which contains all
scripts, styles and artwork and can be opened directly from disk. Use a local
HTTP origin to check saved preferences because browser storage differs on file
URLs.

Run a version 1 replay with:

```sh
npm run --silent replay -- PATH
```

A valid replay prints only its final snapshot JSON to stdout and exits 0. Invalid
or unreadable input prints a message to stderr, keeps stdout empty and exits
nonzero. The [reproduction specification](docs/reproducibility.md) describes board
codes, snapshots and replays.

The pure rules, generation and format validators live in `src/game`. Browser
session effects belong in `src/game/session`, board navigation and cards in
`src/game/board`, and controls in `src/game/controls`. `src/Game.tsx` composes them.
Focused tests sit beside their behavior; full browser journeys belong in `tests`.
The app, Node tools and tests each have a separate strict TypeScript project.

Verification so far uses Node 26.12.1, npm 11.20.0, Playwright 1.64.1 and Chromium
156.0.8078.4. Chromium was launched headlessly and reported that exact version.

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Locked install (`npm ci --no-audit --no-fund`) | Passed, 50 packages |
| `npm run typecheck` | Passed, all three compiler projects |
| `npm test` | Passed, 114 tests in five files |
| Replay CLI example and invalid input | Passed, included in unit tests |
| Complete app build and browser journeys | Pending implementation of the UI |

The full named combination is not yet called tested because the complete app
build and browser journeys remain. A screen reader has not been used. Automated
accessibility-tree evidence and final command results will be recorded after the
browser journeys. Spoken output and real-device touch long press remain user
acceptance checks as defined in the specification.
